[ Incoming Link ]
       │
       ▼
1. Layer 1 (Physical)      ──► Converts incoming light (fiber) or voltage into binary bits.
       │
       ▼
2. Layer 2 (Data Link)     ──► Checks CRC error checksum, verifies its own MAC, 
                               and STRIPS the old Layer 2 header.
       │
       ▼
3. Layer 3 (Network)       ──► 1. Decrements TTL by 1 (drops packet if TTL = 0).
                               2. Reads Destination IP (142.250.190.46).
                               3. Looks up the next hop in its Routing Table.
       │
       ▼
4. Layer 2 (Re-wrapping)   ──► WRAPS the packet in a BRAND NEW Layer 2 frame:
                               • Source MAC = This router's exit port MAC.
                               • Destination MAC = Next router's input port MAC.
       │
       ▼
5. Layer 1 (Transmission)  ──► Converts bits into laser light/voltage and sends it out.
